Lay-What: A browser message the hub refuses is still refused the same way.
Lay-How: The refusal is written by one helper, called from each place the send used to write it.
Lay-Why: The send function had grown past the line limit, which blocked the allow-list change from landing.
Tech-What: wuiRefuse logs the refusal and writes the error frame, including the agent name on sender_not_allowed.
Tech-How: wuiSend calls wuiRefuse at every refusal; the allow-list check still runs after routing and before any store write.
Tech-Why: The clean-code gate rejects a new function over 80 lines, and wuiSend was 87.
